---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Base title="Privacy policy" description="What Ecozenin collects when you register a warranty, and why.">
  <div class="wrap page">
    <div class="page-head">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated October 8, 2026</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        This site is run by {site.legalName}. It collects personal information in one place only: the warranty
        registration form.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your name and email address.</li>
        <li>The product you registered and its purchase date.</li>
        <li>Whether you asked to hear about new products.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The site doesn't use advertising or tracking cookies.</p>

      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To keep a record of your warranty and handle any claim.</li>
        <li>To email you about new products, only if you ticked that box. Every such email has an unsubscribe link.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We don't sell your information or share it for anyone else's marketing.</p>

      <h2>Who handles it for us</h2>
      <p>
        Registrations are stored with Google Firebase, which also hosts this site. It processes the information only
        on our instructions.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep your registration for the length of the warranty and up to two years after it ends, in case of a
        late question about a claim.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a> to see, correct or delete your
        registration, or to stop marketing emails. We act on requests within 30 days.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
